nd therefore attainable precision within a fixed budget; they do not make a completed snapshotCOUNT approximate. Concurrent writes\/replica lag can change the represented time\/population and must not be conflated with estimator error. More sample pages\/ANALYZE does not guarantee monotonic accuracy and has separate maintenance impact.\",\n        \"implementation\": \"Root added isolated bench\/accuracy_frontier.py plus01c-ACCURACY-COST and01d-ACCURACY-SERVICE-100 (.versions8.4.13\/.encrypted\/.outputs). No active imported source was edited. Code is prepared, NOT DB-executed. Review\/fix these scripts rather than duplicate.01c uses seven fixtures xfive seeds x3targets, fullCOUNT paired comparisons, target-specific predeclared looks and same alpha.01d uses100-column TDE with control\/exact\/3%\/10%, index absent\/present, indexed\/nonindexed writes x3repeats=48arms.5% service is explicitly unmeasured; static includes it. Pure arithmetic verifies each first look can meet its target at zero variance; static closure includes new module and sampling dependencies. Both new wrappers honor the review-only aggregate guard (exit3, never success) and declare their required .outputs. Final all has no aggregate cap.\",\n        \"interpretation\": \"Compare accuracy, elapsed time, read volume and service impact rather than require only3%. Include exactCOUNT at0% error. Choose the most favorable method within the accepted error, freshness and service budget;10% is not an unconditional guarantee for arbitrary unknown tables.\",\n        \"newExperiment\": \"Review and run the isolated implementation named in implementation after the current owner ends. Retain hypotheses and proper confidence\/look allocation. Repair demonstrated issues or split if20min is insufficient; do not duplicate experiments or infer unobserved service effects.\",\n        \"reporting\": \"Give a compact condition-by-method comparison with accuracy\/freshness\/cost\/limitations and recommended paths. Distin