B experiment remains. See coverage-interruption.json and coverage-interrupted-run.log. Proceed with one Sol author then corrected white mise run all; unmeasured0k\/0l and incomplete0h\/0j remain required scope.\",\n        \"First exact mise run all failed before reset at Ruby parsing, producing NO new DB measurement. Actual guarded Riela probe confirms task mise exec fixes selection from2.6.10 to3.4.10. Raw evidence-size projection and stale-summary attribution also need bounded fixes before retry. See phaseSpecificWork\/fixes; retain full primary-scale and tolerance scope and all raw samples.\",\n        \"LATEST USER STEERING: latest Ruby is fine. Root installed official latest stable4.0.9, pinned mise.toml4.0.9, changed all5tasks to explicit mise exec, and changed command node to run-white-all.sh bootstrap. Actual guarded Riela latest probe confirms BOTH launcher and child4.0.9. Syntax\/project workflow checks pass; real all still pending. Do not restore3.4 or legacy2.6 support. Finish raw-artifact\/freshness\/cache\/launch-chain regressions, then retry all.\"\n      ],\n      \"latestAccuracySteering\": {\n        \"additionalServicePriority\": \"Because actual100-column3%-target sampling exhausted the1s service budget in all6 no-small-index arms, include a minimal bounded100-column TDE under-load comparison at relaxed10% (plus matched control and existing3% evidence). Test whether reduced draws actually improve budget\/precision outcomes, rather than infer from static checkpoints.5% can be static if a full service factorial would add little. Split scripts within20min limits; avoid an exhaustive redundant factorial.\",\n        \"conditionMechanisms\": \"Distinguish effects on statistical accuracy, cost under a fixed budget, and freshness. Key-space sparsity\/cell-density variance affect sampling interval convergence; page-level row-size\/density heterogeneity, stats sample pages and staleness affect metadata error. A small index, cache, TDE, row width and MVCC